{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-points}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0ee39ccac9a1e06f9564eaf7bf28342699296d548ddaf7c9a371c67bac9bf9d2", "source_text": "Points of algebraic stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:72cede6151b81658a9f963127ec9f19ce3fd9d9dfeb2934f2f140b764dacbbd3", "unit_id": "tag:04XE:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$K, L$", "MATH_0003": "$p : \\Spec(K) \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$q : \\Spec(L) \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$p$", "MATH_0006": "$q$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Omega$", "MATH_0008": "$2$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(\\Omega) \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\Spec(L) \\ar[d]^q \\\\\n\\Spec(K) \\ar[r]^p &\n\\mathcal{X}.\n}\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8122b54510e237463f29d9f50f1bd89ff5926730624001bea327d96e220f3dcc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3603d16f4805cb1bb33cf525d53ed681a1c3bb82a510b1cd24be454e1b90f8a3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack. Let <MATH_0002> be two fields\nand let <MATH_0003> and\n<MATH_0004> be morphisms.\nWe say that <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> are <TEXTITOPEN_0001>equivalent<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if there exists a\nfield <MATH_0007> and a <MATH_0008>-commutative diagram\n<MATH_0009>\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2bd89d6ed7c9dc47958cfb6bdd3dce63323c3cc298b6950bb854c76495d1df08", "unit_id": "tag:04XE:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-equivalence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0002d42c2adc9172acb55958a77085974084083df107126b40344a331769e8cc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fbae6bcd5315695e0e930e75675be64ac3c4cd80d910ba34870ac799531be23f", "source_text": "The notion above does indeed define an equivalence relation on\nmorphisms from spectra of fields into the algebraic stack <MATH_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e0a079f0763b4a3463900cafd4367371aa75827821c01698192a7dfc5e45bd28", "unit_id": "tag:04XF:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(\\Omega) \\ar[r]_b \\ar[d]_a &\n\\Spec(L) \\ar[d]^q & \\Spec(\\Omega') \\ar[l]^{b'} \\ar[d]^{a'} \\\\\n\\Spec(K) \\ar[r]^p &\n\\mathcal{X} &\n\\Spec(K') \\ar[l]_{p'}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "MATH_0003": "$p$", "MATH_0004": "$p'$", "MATH_0005": "$2$", "MATH_0006": "$p$", "MATH_0007": "$p'$", "MATH_0008": "$q$", "MATH_0009": "$x$", "MATH_0010": "$x'$", "MATH_0011": "$y$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\Spec(K)$", "MATH_0014": "$\\Spec(K')$", "MATH_0015": "$\\Spec(L)$", "MATH_0016": "$2$", "MATH_0017": "$\\alpha : a^*x \\to b^*y$", "MATH_0018": "$\\alpha' : (a')^*x' \\to (b')^*y$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0020": "$\\Spec(\\Omega)$", "MATH_0021": "$\\Spec(\\Omega')$", "MATH_0022": "$\\Omega''$", "MATH_0023": "$\\Omega \\to \\Omega''$", "MATH_0024": "$\\Omega' \\to \\Omega''$", "MATH_0025": "$L$", "MATH_0026": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n& \\Spec(\\Omega'') \\ar[ld]_c \\ar[d]^{q'} \\ar[rd]^{c'} \\\\\n\\Spec(\\Omega) \\ar[r]_b \\ar[d]_a &\n\\Spec(L) \\ar[d]^q & \\Spec(\\Omega') \\ar[l]^{b'} \\ar[d]^{a'} \\\\\n\\Spec(K) \\ar[r]^p &\n\\mathcal{X} &\n\\Spec(K') \\ar[l]_{p'}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0027": "$$\n(q')^*(\\alpha')^{-1} \\circ (q')^*\\alpha :\n(a \\circ c)^*x\n\\longrightarrow\n(a' \\circ c')^*x'\n$$", "MATH_0028": "$\\Spec(\\Omega'')$", "MATH_0029": "$p$", "MATH_0030": "$p'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebraic-section-2-yoneda}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5b8bb9b623aa420c934a7910803184b0fc9ac2cac03174dfb67df981d585060b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4d07af48c52ca200fe48f50df44ea9d8118f281361091d77c08560ba50dc2eb6", "source_text": "It is clear that the relation is reflexive and symmetric.\nHence we have to prove that it is transitive. This comes down\nto the following: Given a diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nwith both squares <MATH_0002>-commutative we have to show that <MATH_0003> is equivalent to\n<MATH_0004>. By the <MATH_0005>-Yoneda lemma (see\nAlgebraic Stacks, Section <REF_0001>)\nthe morphisms <MATH_0006>, <MATH_0007>, and <MATH_0008> are given by objects\n<MATH_0009>, <MATH_0010>, and <MATH_0011> in the fibre categories of <MATH_0012> over\n<MATH_0013>, <MATH_0014>, and <MATH_0015>. The\n<MATH_0016>-commutativity of the squares means that there are isomorphisms\n<MATH_0017> and <MATH_0018>\nin the fibre categories\nof <MATH_0019> over <MATH_0020> and <MATH_0021>.\nChoose any field <MATH_0022> and embeddings\n<MATH_0023> and <MATH_0024> agreeing on <MATH_0025>.\nThen we can extend the diagram above to\n<MATH_0026>\nwith commutative triangles and\n<MATH_0027>\nis an isomorphism in the fibre category over <MATH_0028>.\nHence <MATH_0029> is equivalent to <MATH_0030> as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bd11f7c2a1dee7763f85f3ebee59554b6566e2d5412be9941cd5cded0f546a6b", "unit_id": "tag:04XF:proof"}
